  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>On the road linking Gassin to Saint-Tropez, Le Treizain beach — also known as Malleribes, after an old tramway stop — offers an open view across the gulf, with Saint-Tropez and Sainte-Maxime in the background. It's one of Gassin's three beaches, with free, year-round access.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Dogs on leash are allowed, confirmed both by Gassin's tourist office and by the Var department's own tourism board (visitvar.fr), which lists Le Treizain among the department's official dog-friendly beaches — owners are asked to pick up after their dog. The beach is accessible year-round, with no booking or entry fee.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: come in late afternoon to enjoy the gulf view with your dog, when the light over Saint-Tropez is at its best.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p><a href="/en/fiche-plage-moune-gassin">La Moune beach</a> is right next door, and the hilltop village of Gassin inland rounds out the visit easily.</p>
    </div>

